# Editing videos

This repository holds two skills: `editing-videos` (any video) and `car-trailer` (a beat-cut trailer or Short from a finished car how-to). There is no other Cursor rule and no `AGENTS.md`.

For a trailer, teaser, promo, Short, Reel or TikTok of a car how-to, read `skills/car-trailer/SKILL.md` and follow it; it runs `scripts/cut.py`, whose lint must pass before the type layer.

For any request to plan, edit, cut, grade, caption, or finish a video — including automotive and how-to footage — read `skills/editing-videos/SKILL.md` first and follow it. Do not improvise a different pipeline. On tool mechanics, the tool's own docs win; on editorial decisions, this skill does.

After the entry file, load only the recipe and references it names for that video. Paths below are relative to `skills/editing-videos/`.

- Core: `references/` (pacing, hook, graphics and text, audio, color, publishing, licenses, tools) and `review-checklist.md`.
- For a music bed on a how-to, follow `references/audio-and-sfx.md` (`Auditioning music for a how-to`).
- A camera how-to keeps 4K when the camera is 4K, takes chapters from the export the reviewer watched, and yields to car-edit on pacing (`references/tools.md`, `references/thumbnail-title-description.md`).
- A Final Cut timeline is written with [fcp-mcp-server](https://github.com/DareDev256/fcp-mcp-server), then the agent stops. The user imports the XML in Final Cut and exports 4K (`references/tools.md`). Panamera's existing `render.py` still imports the old dreliq9 `fcp_mcp` package; new work must not copy that pattern.
- One recipe: `recipes/talking-head.md`, `recipes/vlog.md`, `recipes/podcast-to-youtube.md`, `recipes/shorts-from-long-form.md`, or `recipes/narrated-screen-tutorial.md`.
- Assets, searched then copied into the video project: `library/`, `graphics/`, and `memes/README.md` before `memes/catalog.json`.

Do not rewrite this skill's editing rules while using it to cut a video.
